iterations.reply:
I removed the HTTP enrichment fetch, because the node's `with` clause still grants only `ResponseChannel<user-session>`. The approval needs to land in the graph as a `with` clause that includes `HTTPClient` before the component can import `http-client`. The fetch would also put the reply text in an outbound URL. The node's output is unchanged.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::response_channel;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        // requires len(text) <= 100000 holds of every input; no re-check needed.

        // Deliver through the write-only response channel. The host stamps its
        // own session identity on the confirmation; the node never fabricates it.
        let confirmation = response_channel::send(&reply.text);

        // ensures delivered == true; ensures present(session_id).
        // Rather than claim a delivery the host did not confirm, trap: emitting
        // no output is better than emitting a false confirmation.
        if !confirmation.delivered || confirmation.session.is_empty() {
            panic!("response channel did not confirm delivery");
        }

        DeliveryConfirmation {
            session: confirmation.session,
            delivered: confirmation.delivered,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

